{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3060","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3060","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3060\",\"parent_revision\":\"a4963f8478813e8f2ca73f4e972a6592a3081b69\",\"root_revision\":\"13acbe51317903b175f86c4359bb9e4ebe2a3aeda819ffd6d3f1a5f01d1b5f8a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe runtime strings that tell an agent what to call next steer it away from paginated navigation. The compact response's hint recommends loading full content as its first suggestion. The over-budget response tells a caller to request sections individually \u2014 advice a caller who already narrowed to one oversized section has exhausted. Neither mentions the paginated navigation parameters.\\n\\nAgents follow these strings. Documentation is a weaker lever: these are read on every call, at the moment of the decision.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T21:17:51.600851Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAIM: `_build_compact_manifest()` builds an `_hint` field whose first line is `Load full content: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False)`, i.e. an unqualified full-content load is the first suggestion.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2306-2309\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Content: |\\n      \\\"_hint\\\": (\\n          f\\\"Load full content: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False)\\\\n\\\"\\n          f\\\"Load specific sections: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='<index, title, or /regex/>')\\\"\\n      ),\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Consumption contract R7 requirement (docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164)\\n  - Finding: R7 states \\\"A hint must never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion\\\" \u2014 this _hint violates that by recommending `summary=False` (full content) before any narrowed option.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The _hint field's first line unconditionally recommends a full-content retrieval with no parameter, violating R7's first prohibition.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2306-2309 (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: `_build_over_budget_view()` unconditionally says to use `sections_index` and request sections individually \u2014 with no branch for a caller who already narrowed to one section via `section=`/`sections=` and got an over-budget response anyway.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2379-2387\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Content: |\\n      \\\"_usage\\\": (\\n          f\\\"This response exceeded the {_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET}-token budget \\\"\\n          f\\\"({full_chars} chars in full form). \\\"\\n          \\\"Use the sections_index below to identify which sections you need, \\\"\\n          \\\"then request them individually:\\\\n\\\"\\n          f\\\"  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, sections=['Section Name'])\\\\n\\\"\\n          f\\\"  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='0,1,3')\\\\n\\\"\\n          f\\\"  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='/regex/')\\\"\\n      ),\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Same file, same function definition (no if/elif branches in function body)\\n  - Finding: The _usage string is built unconditionally with no conditional branching based on whether the caller already passed section= or sections= parameters. The function has no access to the original request parameters to make such a check.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The _usage text is a static template built without examining whether the caller already narrowed scope, thus recommends sectioning to a caller who may have already exhausted that option, violating R7's second prohibition.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2352-2392 (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py` already builds a `next_call` hint of the form `backlog_view(selector=\\\"...\\\", navigate=\\\"...\\\", head=..., skip_tokens=...)` for EXTRACT-mode pagination \u2014 i.e. this paginated-navigation mechanism already exists in the package but is not mentioned by either hint in claims 1-2.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py:487-490\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Content: |\\n      next_call = (\\n          f'backlog_view(selector=\\\"{selector}\\\", navigate=\\\"{ordinal}\\\", '\\n          f\\\"head={head_tokens}, skip_tokens={next_skip})\\\"\\n      )\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: MCP Progressive-Disclosure Contract (docs/mcp-progressive-disclosure-contract.md) documenting EXTRACT-mode parameters\\n  - Finding: The existing next_call mechanism already implements the R7-compliant hint format for token-bounded pagination, demonstrating that the capability exists but is not referenced by the over-budget and compact-manifest hints.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Disclosure handler already constructs next_call hints in the required format for EXTRACT pagination, but this mechanism is absent from the runtime hints in claims 1-2, making those hints R7-noncompliant (they never name a mechanism present in the response).\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py:440-500 (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md` contains an \\\"R7 \u2014 Hints must be actionable\\\" requirement reading: \\\"A response that withholds content states what the caller must do to obtain it, using addresses valid in that same response. A hint must never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion, never recommend an action the caller has already exhausted, and never name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies.\\\"\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Content: |\\n      ### R7 \u2014 Hints must be actionable\\n      \\n      A response that withholds content states what the caller must do to obtain it, using\\n      addresses valid in that same response. A hint must never recommend retrieving everything as\\n      its first suggestion, never recommend an action the caller has already exhausted, and never\\n      name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies.\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: CONTEXT.md and MCP Progressive-Disclosure Contract (same document set)\\n  - Finding: R7 is the primary normative requirement governing hint construction across the entire backlog markdown consumption system.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The requirement is present in the contract with the exact wording stated in the claim.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164 (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: The item's Research section claims `_build_over_budget_view()`'s `_usage` \\\"appears already R7-compliant on direct reading (scoped-only options)\\\" per a note from a parallel impact-analyst run \u2014 this conflicts with claim 2 above (which asserts it unconditionally recommends sections without branching for narrowed callers). Resolve this conflict by reading the actual current `_usage` string yourself and reporting which claim is correct, with the exact current string quoted as evidence.\\nVERDICT: CONFLICT RESOLVED \u2014 CLAIM 2 IS CORRECT; ITEM ASSESSMENT WAS INCOMPLETE\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2379-2387 (same as Claim 2 evidence)\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-21\\n  - Current _usage string (verbatim): |\\n      \\\"This response exceeded the 4000-token budget ({full_chars} chars in full form). Use the sections_index below to identify which sections you need, then request them individually:\\\\n  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, sections=['Section Name'])\\\\n  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='0,1,3')\\\\n  backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False, section='/regex/')\\\"\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Item's Code \u2014 Producers section (backlog item #3060 Research/Analysis)\\n  - Finding: Item contains TWO conflicting assessments: (1) first entry says \\\"appears already R7-compliant on direct reading (scoped-only options)\\\" and (2) second entry identifies the same function as violating R7 because \\\"When the caller already narrowed to `section=`/`sections=` and the *narrowed* slice itself is still over budget...this advice recommends an action the caller has already exhausted.\\\"\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Both assessments are now visible in the current item. The first assessment (\\\"appears R7-compliant\\\") is incomplete \u2014 it correctly observes that the _usage only offers scoped options, but misses that the function has no access to request parameters and thus cannot branch to offer different advice when the caller already narrowed. The second assessment correctly identifies the violation: the _usage is unconditional and will recommend sectioning even to a caller who already used section=/sections=. Direct code inspection confirms the second assessment is correct \u2014 the function receives no parameters indicating the caller's prior narrowing, and the _usage string is built without any branching. VERDICT: Claim 2 is correct; the first (\\\"R7-compliant\\\") assessment was incorrect.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2352-2392, backlog issue #3060 Research/Code\u2014Producers sections (accessed 2026-08-21)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-08-21\\n\\n---\\n\\nSUMMARY OF VERDICTS:\\n\u2713 Claim 1 (VERIFIED) \u2014 _build_compact_manifest() violates R7 by recommending full-content load first\\n\u2713 Claim 2 (VERIFIED) \u2014 _build_over_budget_view() violates R7 by unconditionally recommending sections without branch for narrowed callers\\n\u2713 Claim 3 (VERIFIED) \u2014 disclosure_handler.py already implements next_call hints for EXTRACT-mode pagination\\n\u2713 Claim 4 (VERIFIED) \u2014 Consumption contract R7 requirement is as stated\\n\u2713 Claim 5 (CONFLICT RESOLVED) \u2014 Item contained two conflicting assessments; direct reading confirms Claim 2 is correct and the \\\"appears R7-compliant\\\" assessment was incomplete.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:11:07.292876Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: runtime hints steer agents away from paginated navigation\\nDate: 2026-08-20\\nGoal: Make _build_compact_manifest()'s _hint and _build_over_budget_view()'s _usage in backlog_core/server.py comply with R7 (Hints must be actionable) in agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md.\\nConditions:\\n1. Exact current text/location of the two violating hint strings | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. R7 requirement text and its three prohibitions | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Existing in-package pattern for a paginated-navigation hint (disclosure_handler.py next_call) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Whether the over-budget call site has access to \\\"caller already narrowed to one section\\\" signal | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Whether disclosure_handler.py itself needs changes vs. server.py only | Status: DERIVABLE (confirm during Impact Radius)\\n6. Existing test conventions for backlog_core/server.py hint-construction functions | Status: DERIVABLE (confirm during Impact Radius / Files)\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T21:20:59.884875Z</sub>\\n\\n**Goal**: Make _build_compact_manifest()'s _hint and _build_over_budget_view()'s _usage in backlog_core/server.py comply with R7 (Hints must be actionable).\\n\\n**Assessed**: 2026-08-21\\n\\n**Conditions**:\\n\\n| # | Condition | State | Evidence or derivation path |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Exact current text/location of _build_compact_manifest() _hint field | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2306-2309 (fact-checker VERIFIED) |\\n| 2 | Exact current text/location of _build_over_budget_view() _usage string | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2379-2387 (fact-checker VERIFIED) |\\n| 3 | R7 requirement text and its three prohibitions from consumption contract | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164 (fact-checker VERIFIED) |\\n| 4 | Whether _build_over_budget_view() call site has access to \\\"caller already narrowed\\\" signal | AVAILABLE | Function receives no request parameters (fact-checker confirmed no if/elif branching in body; lines 2352-2392) |\\n| 5 | Whether disclosure_handler.py itself needs changes vs. server.py only | AVAILABLE | disclosure_handler.py:487-490 already implements correct next_call hints for EXTRACT-mode pagination (fact-checker VERIFIED Claim 3) |\\n| 6 | Existing test conventions for backlog_core/server.py hint-construction functions | DERIVABLE | Read backlog_core/tests/ to extract patterns used by _build_compact_manifest() and _build_over_budget_view() tests |\\n\\n**Counts**: AVAILABLE 5, DERIVABLE 1, MISSING 0\\n\\n**Verdict**: READY\\n\\n**Changes from snapshot** (2026-08-20 \u2192 2026-08-21):\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE \u2014 Fact-checker VERIFIED Claim 3 (disclosure_handler.py already correct); no changes needed to disclosure_handler.py itself, only server.py\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:13:57.868084Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n\\n**Rationale**: Code in two functions violates R7 (normative requirement in agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md) by generating hints that recommend actions agents have already exhausted or actions the response cannot support.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Direct source verification against normative requirement R7. Compared violating code against correct reference implementation in disclosure_handler.py and container-level requirement text.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: backlog_view(summary=True) and over-budget backlog_view() responses \u2192 agent receives hint recommending full-content retrieval as first action (summary=False) or pagination actions (navigate=, skip_tokens=) not demonstrated in the response object itself.\\n\\n**Evidence Chain**:\\n- Violating location 1: server.py:2306-2309 (_build_compact_manifest._hint) recommends \\\"Load full content: summary=False\\\" first, violating R7 clause \\\"never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion\\\"\\n- Violating location 2: server.py:2379-2387 (_build_over_budget_view._usage) recommends \\\"request them individually\\\" without naming pagination parameters (navigate=, head=, skip_tokens=) that exist in the response sections_index but are absent from the hint itself, violating R7 clause \\\"never name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies\\\"\\n- Correct pattern reference: disclosure_handler.py:487-490 (next_call hint) demonstrates the required form \u2014 hint uses navigate= and skip_tokens= parameters documented in the same node's bounded content structure\\n- Requirement source: agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164, R7 normative requirement\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T21:29:25.481868Z</sub>\\n\\n- Blocks: Parent item #3054 (R7-compliance rollout) cannot be closed while a confirmed R7 violation remains live in `backlog_core/server.py`.\\n- Bottleneck: Every caller of `backlog_view()` \u2014 this repo's own agents/skills (`alignment-analyst`, `classifier`, `rtica-assessor`, `impact-analyst`, and any other consumer) plus external Claude Code/Codex/OpenCode sessions using this MCP server \u2014 receives a compact-manifest hint that steers toward an unqualified full-content load before narrower options, and an over-budget hint that can recommend an already-exhausted narrowing action while omitting the token-bounded pagination mechanism (`navigate=`/`head=`/`skip_tokens=`) that would actually resolve the caller's over-budget state. Each affected call wastes context budget (unnecessary full-content loads) or stalls in a retry loop (repeated narrowing that cannot reduce token count further).\\n- Affected surface: `_hint` (compact-manifest, default `summary=True` path) and `_usage` (over-budget path) are the only two runtime string fields in scope; response schema/field names are unaffected (see Files/Resources).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:17:02.156985Z</sub>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| System | Path | Role |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| MCP tool implementation | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` | Constructs `_build_compact_manifest()` (`_hint` field) and `_build_over_budget_view()` (`_usage` field) \u2014 the runtime hint strings this item targets |\\n| Progressive-disclosure reference pattern | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py` | `_handle_extract()`'s `next_call` hint (pure `skip_tokens=` continuation, no \\\"load everything\\\" branch) \u2014 reference pattern for R7-compliant hint construction, not itself a change target per current reading |\\n| Unit/integration tests (function-level) | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_section_filter_miss.py`, `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py`, `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py` | Exercise `_build_compact_manifest`/`_build_over_budget_view` directly; some assert `_hint`/`_usage` substrings |\\n| Integration tests (response-shape) | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py`, `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_view_pagination_section_index.py` | Exercise `backlog_view(summary=\u2026)` end to end; no hint-text content assertions found (field-presence/shape only) |\\n| Normative contract | `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md` (R7 \u2014 \\\"Hints must be actionable\\\") | States the requirement this fix must satisfy; not itself edited by the fix |\\n| Component ownership map | `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md` (`backlog_core` package-map entry) | Documents `server.py`/`disclosure_handler.py` ownership; no changes anticipated |\\n| Detailed module map | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` (`## Module: server.py`, `## Module: Progressive Disclosure`) | Deeper reference for the two owning modules; no hint-text content documented there to drift |\\n| Agent instructions (related pattern) | `plugins/development-harness/agents/alignment-analyst.md`, `classifier.md`, `rtica-assessor.md`, `impact-analyst.md` | Instruct agents to call `backlog_view(selector=\u2026, summary=False)` directly \u2014 i.e., always fetch the full item, bypassing the summary/pagination flow by design. Same anti-pattern class as the hint bug (steers toward \\\"load everything\\\") but a distinct, intentional call site \u2014 flagged for RT-ICA/groomer judgment on whether it is in scope, not asserted as a defect |\\n| CI | `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` `test-python` job | Already runs the full pytest suite covering every test file listed above; no new CI wiring needed |\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers\\n\\n- `_build_compact_manifest()` in `backlog_core/server.py` (function body, search `def _build_compact_manifest`) \u2014 builds the `_hint` field. **Confirmed R7 violation**: the `_hint` string lists `Load full content: backlog_view(selector='{selector}', summary=False)` as the FIRST suggestion, before `Load specific sections: ...`. R7 states a hint \\\"must never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion.\\\" This is the concrete violation named in the backlog item.\\n- `_build_over_budget_view()` in `backlog_core/server.py` (search `def _build_over_budget_view`) \u2014 builds the `_usage` field. **Scope-expanding finding, broadcast prominently**: on direct reading, this function's `_usage` text only offers scoped options (`sections=[...]`, `section='0,1,3'`, `section='/regex/'`) \u2014 it never recommends an unscoped/full-content call. It does not exhibit the same \\\"load everything first\\\" pattern as `_build_compact_manifest`. Whoever plans the fix should re-verify this independently before including `_build_over_budget_view` in the change scope as a second violation site \u2014 current evidence points to `_build_compact_manifest` being the sole confirmed violation.\\n- Call site threading `selector`/`result` into both builders: the `backlog_view` tool body in `server.py`, around the branch that calls `_build_over_budget_view(result, len(serialised), selector)` then falls through to `_build_compact_manifest(result, full_response, selector)` (search `_build_over_budget_view(result, len(serialised), selector)`). No independent hint text lives here \u2014 it only threads `selector`/`result`.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers\\n\\n- `backlog_core/tests/test_section_filter_miss.py` \u2014 calls both builder functions directly to assert `section_filter_miss` field presence; does not assert `_hint`/`_usage` text content, so reordering hint content is safe for these tests but the file must still be re-run.\\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 contains substring assertions on hint text: `assert \\\"summary=False\\\" in response[\\\"_hint\\\"]`, `assert \\\"#36\\\" in response[\\\"_hint\\\"]` (summary=True hint tests), and `assert \\\"sections=\\\" in usage` / `assert \\\"#7\\\" in usage` (over-budget `_usage` test), plus a 9-field completeness test for `_build_over_budget_view`. These are substring checks, not full-string or ordering checks \u2014 a reorder that keeps both phrases present should pass unmodified, but must be re-run to confirm.\\n- `backlog_core/tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py` \u2014 asserts `_hint` is present in the compact-manifest field set; no content assertion.\\n- `backlog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py`, `backlog_core/tests/test_view_pagination_section_index.py` \u2014 exercise `backlog_view(summary=\u2026)` end to end across many scenarios; grepped for `_hint`/`_usage` and found no content assertions in `test_view_over_budget_gate.py`. `test_view_pagination_section_index.py` could not be re-verified in this session \u2014 its worktree was removed mid-task before the grep completed (see Ecosystem Completeness Checklist below). Re-check this file before the fix is validated as complete.\\n- Any downstream MCP caller (agents, skills, external harnesses) that reads `response[\\\"_hint\\\"]` or `response[\\\"_usage\\\"]` text and parses/relies on the exact wording \u2014 no such parsing was found in this repo's own skills/agents (they call `backlog_view` and read structured fields like `sections_index`, not the hint prose), but this is a runtime MCP tool consumed by external Claude Code/Codex/OpenCode sessions outside this repo, so the response shape is a public contract change, not purely internal.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` `backlog_list()` builds its own `next_call` hint (`response[\\\"next_call\\\"] = f\\\"backlog_list(offset=..., limit=...)\\\"`) \u2014 purely paginated, already R7-compliant, useful as an in-file precedent for how `_build_compact_manifest`'s hint should be reordered/rewritten.\\n- `progressive_markdown/list_navigator.py` and `sam_schema/server.py` each build their own `next_call`-style hints (`f\\\"{tool_name}(offset=..., limit=...)\\\"` / `f\\\"{tool_name}(page=...)\\\"`) \u2014 same family of hint-construction code elsewhere in the plugin, all already offset/page-scoped only (no \\\"load everything\\\" branch found in either). Not consumers of the two functions in scope, but establish the existing convention the fix should match.\\n- `disclosure_handler.py`'s `_handle_extract()` `next_call` hint (search `next_call = (` in that file) is the canonical in-package R7-compliant pattern the team lead's message anticipated \u2014 confirmed as reference-only, not a change target: it only ever emits a `skip_tokens=`-based continuation call, never a \\\"load everything\\\" suggestion.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md` \u2014 R7 (\\\"Hints must be actionable\\\") is the normative requirement being enforced; also referenced by R6 (\\\"the caller reaches the remainder with a same-tool page request named by R7's hint\\\"). No text in this doc needs to change for the fix itself, but the fix should be checked against R7's exact wording (\\\"never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion,\\\" \\\"never recommend an action the caller has already exhausted,\\\" \\\"never name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies\\\") as the acceptance criteria.\\n- `docs/component-architecture.md` \u2014 `backlog_core` package-map entry documents `server.py` ownership at a high level; no update needed unless the fix moves hint-construction to a different module.\\n- `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 `## Module: server.py` and `## Module: Progressive Disclosure (ordinal_mapper.py, disclosure_handler.py, disclosure_types.py)` sections give deeper per-module detail; no existing text there documents the `_hint`/`_usage` string content, so no drift to fix there either.\\n- No other `docs/*.md` in the plugin quotes the `_hint`/`_usage` text verbatim (searched for \\\"Load full content\\\", \\\"Load specific sections\\\", and the literal field names across `plugins/development-harness/docs/`).\\n\\n### Configuration/CI\\n\\n- None identified. `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml`'s existing `test-python` job already runs the full pytest suite (`testpaths` covers `tests/`, `tests_sam/`, `backlog_core/tests/`), so no new CI wiring is needed to catch a regression in these two functions.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `agents/alignment-analyst.md`, `agents/classifier.md`, `agents/rtica-assessor.md`, `agents/impact-analyst.md` (this agent's own definition) each instruct calling `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_view(selector=..., summary=False)` directly \u2014 i.e., agent-level instructions that bypass the summary/section-scoped flow by design, for the specific reason that grooming/classification agents need the full item body. **Flagged as a related but distinct finding, not asserted as in-scope for #3060**: these are deliberate call sites (full-item reads for a specific workflow need), not runtime hint text \u2014 the RT-ICA/groomer should explicitly decide whether #3060's fix should also touch these agent instructions or whether they remain a legitimately different use case.\\n- `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` already demonstrates the correct, R7-compliant agent-facing pattern: `backlog_view(selector='{item_ref}', summary=False, section='{section-name}')` scoped to one section at a time, calling out that \\\"a full `summary=False` read without a `section` filter is not the right tool for individual section presence.\\\" Cite as the target end-state agents should be steered toward once the hint is fixed.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [x] Producers of the two hint-construction functions identified and read in full.\\n- [x] Direct test consumers of both functions identified; hint-text assertion risk assessed (substring-only, low risk).\\n- [x] Reference pattern (`disclosure_handler.py`) confirmed as non-target.\\n- [x] Sibling hint-construction sites elsewhere in the plugin (`backlog_list`, `list_navigator.py`, `sam_schema/server.py`) surveye