True` \u2192 `navigate=<ordinal>` \u2192 `navigate=<ordinal>+head=N`, iterating via `next_call`) as the \\\"new, three-layer\\\" pattern, alongside the \\\"legacy, still supported\\\" `summary=`/`section=` pattern. This confirms the paginated params the two violating hints should point to already exist and are already the documented preferred path.\\n- **`backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py`**, `_handle_extract()` (~lines 448\u2013498): the in-package reference pattern for an R7-compliant hint \u2014 builds `next_call` only when `bounded.truncated` (never recommends an exhausted action), using the caller's actual `selector` and pointing at `navigate=`/`head=`/`skip_tokens=`. This is the pattern the fix should reuse, not itself a change target \u2014 confirms the Research section's cross-check.\\n- **`backlog_core/server.py`**, `backlog_list()`'s `next_call` hint (~line 2268): separate, already-compliant pattern \u2014 only set `if has_more`, so it never recommends an exhausted action. Not a change target; confirms the Research section's claim that no other call site in `backlog_core/` violates R7.\\n\\n### Tests (file-level references requiring coordinated update)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py::test_backlog_view_summary_true_returns_compact_manifest` (~line 1004): asserts `\\\"summary=False\\\" in response[\\\"_hint\\\"]`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py::test_backlog_view_summary_true_hint_contains_selector` (~line 1046): asserts the exact caller-supplied selector string appears verbatim in `_hint`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py::test_build_over_budget_view_usage_mentions_sections_param` (~line 3898): asserts `\\\"sections=\\\" in usage` and the selector (`\\\"#7\\\"`) appears in `_usage`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py::test_build_over_budget_view_includes_all_nine_fields` (~line 3853): pins the *field-name* set (`number, title, priority, status, description, sections_index, _over_budget, _full_chars, _usage`) \u2014 unaffected by content changes inside `_usage`, only by adding/removing top-level fields.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/integration/test_backlog_view_disclosure_tool.py`, `_PASSTHROUGH_LEGACY_KEYS` frozenset (~line 103) and its assertion (~line 537): pins the exact *key set* of the PASSTHROUGH `summary=True` response, including `_hint`. Rewriting the `_hint` string in place is safe; adding a new top-level key is not \u2014 it would fail this pinned-key assertion and require a coordinated test update.\\n\\nNone of these tests assert the full literal hint text \u2014 all assert substrings (`summary=False`, the selector, `sections=`) or field/key names. A fix that rewrites the hint content while preserving those substrings and the existing key names needs no test changes; a fix that removes any asserted substring, or adds/removes a top-level field, requires updating the corresponding test(s) above in the same change.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`, R7 (\\\"Hints must be actionable\\\"): the normative requirement this fix satisfies. No edit needed to R7 itself \u2014 it states the contract, not the current hint text.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/mcp-progressive-disclosure-contract.md`: checked \u2014 does not quote or describe the literal `_hint`/`_usage` strings, no edit required.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`: places `backlog_core/server.py` as the component boundary for MCP-facing response construction (confirmed at the `publish_artifact()` reference, ~line 133); no separate architecture-doc edit required for this fix.\\n\\n### Configuration/CI\\n\\nNone identified. No config file, lint rule, or CI workflow encodes or asserts these hint strings.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\nNone identified. Repo-wide grep for `_hint`, `_usage`, `